WEBVTT

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:09.980
This is a work of fiction based on research into the period in which it is set. The people,
 organization, laws, and names that appear in it have no relation to any in the real world.

00:01:57.760 --> 00:01:59.640
Fight seriously.

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:00.850
But...

00:02:00.850 --> 00:02:02.980
Is it because I'm human?

00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:05.770
Yes.

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:08.520
That softness will get your friends killed.

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:15.490
All right.

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:35.590
Look.

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:38.180
You can't even beat a human like me.

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:41.520
Colonel Maeda!

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:43.810
A body was found in Yoshiwara.

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:44.810
It's a vamp.

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:46.400
On my way.

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:49.270
Dawn already?

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:50.860
Stand by until night.

00:02:56.780 --> 00:03:00.990
Unknown Song

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:12.550
Choyaro, a large Yoshiwara brothel.

00:03:12.550 --> 00:03:14.920
The prostitute's name was Otama?

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:16.630
Missing for two days.

00:03:16.630 --> 00:03:20.050
We were called due to
the discoloration of the body.

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:30.690
Have undercover agents
search the area around Choyaro.

00:03:30.690 --> 00:03:32.940
We'll send Zero in tonight.

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:35.240
It's gone.

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:38.320
My Yoshiwara poisoning article
is gone! Why, boss?!

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:42.240
Our readers are trend-chasing modern girls.

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:45.790
Besides, what's so unusual
about a dead prostitute?

00:03:45.790 --> 00:03:50.290
But there could be secret or forbidden
love involved, couldn't there?

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:54.590
The story got hushed up. From above.

00:03:54.590 --> 00:03:55.880
Who do you mean?

00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:57.420
I mean the military.

00:03:57.420 --> 00:03:59.640
I don't want to get crushed.

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:00.470
But...

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:02.510
"Buts" are for ash trays.

00:04:02.510 --> 00:04:05.850
Now, back to work.
I need you at the Imperial Hotel.

00:04:05.850 --> 00:04:08.190
The Frank Lloyd Wright building?

00:04:08.190 --> 00:04:10.810
At the completion ceremony in September,

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:16.190
a cosmetics dealer will be advertising
a line of British perfumes in the arcade.

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:19.410
Umm, can I ask you something?

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:20.410
What?

00:04:20.410 --> 00:04:24.790
Can I charge the paper for
roast beef at the Imperial Hotel?

00:04:24.790 --> 00:04:26.160
Idiot.

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:29.580
As for Yoshiwara,

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:31.420
I got it all hushed up.

00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:33.290
Sorry for the trouble.

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:37.050
Don't mention it; it's all I can do to help you.

00:04:37.050 --> 00:04:40.340
I understand. About the budget as well.

00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:43.470
I'm truly sorry.

00:04:43.470 --> 00:04:46.180
And when does it start?

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:48.980
Your budget will be halved as of next year.

00:04:48.980 --> 00:04:52.860
I won't even be able to pay those
young men enough to feed themselves.

00:04:52.860 --> 00:04:57.150
The Vampire Unit Plan is the biggest money sink.

00:04:57.150 --> 00:04:59.610
You'll have to freeze it.

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:01.490
That's a problem.

00:05:01.490 --> 00:05:04.320
This isn't limited to special forces.

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:09.660
They're planning to reduce
the whole military by 100,000 men.

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:13.630
Are you abandoning the plan
to fold us into the secret service?

00:05:13.630 --> 00:05:17.250
You should consider this year your time limit.

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:23.890
If you don't produce notable results,
Special Forces Unit 16 will be disbanded.

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:26.970
That really is a problem.

00:05:28.270 --> 00:05:29.850
So, this is Yoshiwara.

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:33.600
It's been synonymous with
a good time since the Edo period.

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:34.980
Wow.

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:37.360
Suwa,

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:40.360
isn't that too flashy for undercover work?

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:42.030
This is normal here.

00:05:42.030 --> 00:05:44.530
It's like another world.

00:05:44.530 --> 00:05:47.910
Colonel, do you know where we should infiltrate?

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:49.790
We narrowed it down to Choyaro.

00:05:49.790 --> 00:05:53.670
Now you'll just have to go in and find the vamp.

00:05:53.670 --> 00:05:55.790
But how will we look for them?

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:56.410
Huh?

00:05:56.410 --> 00:05:59.920
We can't tell who's a vampire and who isn't.

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:02.720
What the hell are you talking about?

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:03.930
Oh, of course!

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:07.220
Kurusu is the highest-ranked vampire in Japan.

00:06:07.220 --> 00:06:08.810
Why does that matter?

00:06:08.810 --> 00:06:12.980
You can tell that we're
vampires, right, Yamagami?

00:06:12.980 --> 00:06:14.650
Why is that?

00:06:14.650 --> 00:06:15.900
You scare me.

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:17.150
Exactly!

00:06:17.150 --> 00:06:20.730
You instinctively fear vampires who outrank you!

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:25.030
Now, Yamagami, take the lead
and look for vampires.

00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:29.370
As the weakest of us all,
it's something only you can do.

00:06:29.370 --> 00:06:32.040
It's a good thing you're unranked.

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:35.120
Isn't that great, Yamagami?

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:37.170
Huh? What's wrong?

00:06:37.170 --> 00:06:39.630
You're all so insensitive!

00:06:39.630 --> 00:06:41.090
Go, Yamagami. That way.

00:06:41.090 --> 00:06:44.380
Don't you start treating me like a dog, too!

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:46.470
Fine! I'll go.

00:06:46.470 --> 00:06:49.810
Vampires probably won't
attack another vampire anyway.

00:06:49.810 --> 00:06:52.180
Who gave you that idea?

00:06:52.180 --> 00:06:52.720
Huh?

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:57.270
To a higher-ranked vampire,
you're nearly human and a tasty treat.

00:06:57.270 --> 00:07:00.110
What?! Is that how you guys see me?!

00:07:00.110 --> 00:07:02.690
Just kidding. We're not cannibals.

00:07:02.690 --> 00:07:05.110
Who would eat <i>you</i>, idiot?

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:06.320
Don't worry!

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:11.240
You're ours Yamagami; we won't
let any other vampires eat you!

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:14.040
I might be in more danger staying here.

00:07:14.040 --> 00:07:17.750
If anything happens, call us with
ultrasonic waves like I taught you.

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:19.380
Umm...

00:07:21.090 --> 00:07:22.460
Like this?

00:07:22.460 --> 00:07:23.510
Yes, that's right.

00:07:23.510 --> 00:07:25.220
Hey, Kurusu!

00:07:25.220 --> 00:07:27.550
What are you doing? Let's go!

00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:34.390
I always wanted to visit the Imperial Hotel!

00:07:34.390 --> 00:07:36.390
It's lovely!

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:40.110
Yes. From England to Yokohama, as planned.

00:07:40.110 --> 00:07:42.980
I've arranged for the highest quality.

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:46.360
Excellent. This will
bring us closer to my ideal.

00:07:46.360 --> 00:07:48.530
I'll be counting on you again.

00:07:48.530 --> 00:07:53.120
Anything you wish.
I, Rufus Glenn, am at your service.

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:54.580
That guy...

00:07:54.580 --> 00:07:56.500
Have I seen him before?

00:07:59.960 --> 00:08:02.380
Hey, you there.

00:08:02.380 --> 00:08:04.630
This is no place for children.

00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:07.260
Or did you sneak in for an allowance?

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:13.060
I may not look it, but I'm a reporter.

00:08:13.060 --> 00:08:17.480
A reporter? Oh, for the paper
running the advertisement.

00:08:17.480 --> 00:08:19.310
So, they sent you.

00:08:19.310 --> 00:08:22.480
I'm Aoi Shirase for the Nitto News!

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:24.480
Get to it, then.

00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:26.440
What's this?

00:08:26.440 --> 00:08:31.280
A captivating perfume, although I
doubt your kind appreciates its quality.

00:08:32.740 --> 00:08:35.910
Once you do, this country will change...

00:08:35.910 --> 00:08:39.250
...into a beautiful country
that suits my ideals.

00:08:40.750 --> 00:08:42.960
Any progress analyzing the contents?

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:46.210
You could call it poisoned V Virus.

00:08:46.210 --> 00:08:47.130
Poisoned?

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:51.010
Used on vampires,
it causes abnormal stimulation.

00:08:51.010 --> 00:08:55.180
I haven't tested what happens
when it enters a human body.

00:08:55.180 --> 00:08:57.020
Care to try it, Colonel?

00:08:57.020 --> 00:08:58.230
There's no need.

00:08:58.230 --> 00:09:01.940
They must be doing that here already.

00:09:01.940 --> 00:09:04.270
Takeuchi, we made it to Choyaro.

00:09:04.270 --> 00:09:07.280
Roger. Be careful.

00:09:07.280 --> 00:09:09.240
They're infiltrating.

00:09:09.240 --> 00:09:10.950
Good. Go.

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:22.750
I am called Akesato.

00:09:22.750 --> 00:09:25.210
Please, be gentle with me.

00:09:29.970 --> 00:09:32.430
Would you care for a pipe?

00:09:32.430 --> 00:09:33.550
I don't smoke.

00:09:33.550 --> 00:09:35.010
Perhaps a game?

00:09:35.010 --> 00:09:36.640
Toraken, or--

00:09:36.640 --> 00:09:38.060
I don't play.

00:09:38.060 --> 00:09:39.350
A song, then?

00:09:39.350 --> 00:09:42.600
Sorry, I don't know any songs.

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:45.310
Then what can I...

00:09:59.950 --> 00:10:02.790
Easy. Don't try too hard.

00:10:02.790 --> 00:10:04.290
What a charming fellow.

00:10:04.290 --> 00:10:05.880
How old are you?

00:10:07.130 --> 00:10:08.210
Three hundred.

00:10:08.210 --> 00:10:11.840
You must be one of those vampires
I've heard so much about.

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:12.800
That's right.

00:10:12.800 --> 00:10:16.220
My, what a charming vampire.

00:10:16.220 --> 00:10:17.760
How old are you?

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:20.270
I've just turned 15.

00:10:20.270 --> 00:10:23.140
A Taisho kid, then. Not my type.

00:10:23.140 --> 00:10:26.110
Surely you were raised
in the Taisho era yourself?

00:10:26.110 --> 00:10:28.480
In the Taisho era? Me? As if.

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:31.740
Do I look crazy for all things Western?

00:10:31.740 --> 00:10:34.490
How funny you are.

00:10:34.490 --> 00:10:36.450
A prostitute at your age.

00:10:36.450 --> 00:10:40.200
You must be more level-headed than most girls.

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:41.410
Is it hard?

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:42.830
I'm used to it now.

00:10:42.830 --> 00:10:49.500
Besides, mister, it's the world outside
that's full of people like vampires.

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:53.130
This is the only place I can call home.

00:10:53.130 --> 00:11:00.060
When I was about your age, a gang
of vampires sucked out all my blood.

00:11:00.060 --> 00:11:02.220
How old are you really?

00:11:02.220 --> 00:11:04.890
Three hundred. I told you.

00:11:04.890 --> 00:11:07.940
Then please take this, Mister Vampire.

00:11:07.940 --> 00:11:10.070
It's my hairpin.

00:11:10.070 --> 00:11:11.980
I don't want it.

00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:14.820
Promise you'll come and return it.

00:11:14.820 --> 00:11:16.910
I can't make that promise.

00:11:16.910 --> 00:11:18.570
This is the red-light district.

00:11:18.570 --> 00:11:22.330
The courteous thing is to say,
"yes," even if it's a lie.

00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:26.120
Fine.

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:30.540
Whoever has your love is a fortunate woman.

00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:32.840
H-Hey, give that back!

00:11:32.840 --> 00:11:33.960
I won't.

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:36.050
I'll lose control.

00:11:45.060 --> 00:11:47.140
So, she fell asleep.

00:11:54.690 --> 00:11:59.280
If I knew any songs,
I could have kept that going longer.

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:02.700
Yamagami found the vampire!

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:08.120
Have a nice dream.

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:17.260
This many vampires on duty, and they got away?!

00:12:17.260 --> 00:12:19.680
One of you is A-class! Inexcusable!

00:12:19.680 --> 00:12:21.220
I'm sorry, sir.

00:12:21.220 --> 00:12:24.930
But how did the vampire know we were there?

00:12:24.930 --> 00:12:27.180
Probably because of Kurusu.

00:12:27.180 --> 00:12:28.480
I'm sorry!

00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:31.480
Then Yamagami will scout alone from now on.

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:34.650
Are you trying to get me killed?

00:12:34.650 --> 00:12:38.530
What happened to the Maeda
who went to that tempura place with us?

00:12:38.530 --> 00:12:44.070
While you were failing to find the vamp,
we got a report of another victim.

00:12:40.910 --> 00:12:45.240
Oh, I wish I could've eaten
that tempura one more time.

00:12:45.240 --> 00:12:49.250
One customer and one
prostitute dead in Yoshiwara.

00:12:49.250 --> 00:12:51.540
Is the autopsy finished, Takeuchi?

00:12:51.540 --> 00:12:55.500
Yes. The bodies were discolored as you'd expect.

00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:58.380
But there was one unexpected detail.

00:12:58.380 --> 00:13:00.800
What was it?

00:13:00.800 --> 00:13:03.260
The sizes of the bite marks

00:13:03.260 --> 00:13:05.310
don’t match.

00:13:17.450 --> 00:13:19.620
Body in a ditch in Higashimachi.

00:13:19.620 --> 00:13:21.420
We sent it to Tsukishima.

00:13:21.420 --> 00:13:22.160
Bite marks?

00:13:22.160 --> 00:13:24.500
Don't match the last two.

00:13:24.500 --> 00:13:27.130
Understood. Keep looking.

00:13:27.130 --> 00:13:28.340
Yes, sir.

00:13:31.800 --> 00:13:34.430
That makes six cases near Yoshiwara.

00:13:34.430 --> 00:13:38.020
The bite marks are from another new vamp.

00:13:38.020 --> 00:13:42.230
There are too many for the vamp
we let escape to be making.

00:13:42.230 --> 00:13:44.350
So, you're really a soldier.

00:13:44.350 --> 00:13:47.150
You again? What's a reporter doing here?

00:13:47.150 --> 00:13:48.980
Chasing this dead-body mystery.

00:13:48.980 --> 00:13:52.990
But why are soldiers on
the case and not the police?

00:13:52.990 --> 00:13:56.160
That's classified. I don't have to answer.

00:13:57.530 --> 00:14:00.830
Colonel Maeda, we found traces of the vamp.

00:14:00.830 --> 00:14:02.870
Understood. On my way.

00:14:04.290 --> 00:14:05.790
Colonel Maeda.

00:14:05.790 --> 00:14:08.500
So, he's a big shot.

00:14:08.500 --> 00:14:12.260
I had no idea that vampires
were so fond of Yoshiwara.

00:14:12.260 --> 00:14:14.300
This must be their base of operations.

00:14:14.300 --> 00:14:16.430
Yes, that seems clear.

00:14:16.430 --> 00:14:18.390
Good luck, Yamagami!

00:14:18.390 --> 00:14:19.600
I know.

00:14:22.810 --> 00:14:24.690
Just talk in falsetto, right?

00:14:24.690 --> 00:14:26.730
Ultrasonic waves.

00:14:26.730 --> 00:14:28.070
Right.

00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:33.950
Where's Suwa?

00:14:33.950 --> 00:14:36.280
Already infiltrating, I think.

00:14:39.610 --> 00:14:43.860
I never thought I'd end up
hunting vampires in Yoshiwara.

00:14:46.710 --> 00:14:48.580
Who's that prostitute?

00:14:48.580 --> 00:14:50.960
She's barefoot and staggering.

00:14:50.960 --> 00:14:53.970
Wait, she's a vampire?

00:14:53.970 --> 00:14:55.010
Hang on.

00:14:55.010 --> 00:14:56.420
Her, too!

00:15:05.730 --> 00:15:08.850
There are this many of them?!

00:15:08.850 --> 00:15:12.610
Yamagami here. I found them! In pursuit.

00:15:12.610 --> 00:15:14.650
Could they hear that?

00:15:14.650 --> 00:15:15.780
Shit!

00:15:15.940 --> 00:15:17.940
Choyaro

00:15:17.110 --> 00:15:18.070
She's gone?

00:15:18.070 --> 00:15:21.650
She said she was ill and
spent the last few days in bed.

00:15:21.650 --> 00:15:25.290
I haven't been able
to find her since last night.

00:15:25.290 --> 00:15:26.750
I see.

00:15:26.750 --> 00:15:30.330
Sir, I have much nicer girls than Akesato.

00:15:30.330 --> 00:15:32.300
Charming girls who take after me.

00:15:32.300 --> 00:15:33.710
I don't want them.

00:15:36.470 --> 00:15:38.130
Any word from Yamagami?

00:15:38.130 --> 00:15:40.220
Nothing yet, right?

00:15:40.220 --> 00:15:41.420
Right.

00:15:41.420 --> 00:15:45.310
Maybe Yamagami couldn't
figure out ultrasonic communication?

00:15:45.310 --> 00:15:49.310
And he's still pursuing them
without any way to contact us?

00:15:49.310 --> 00:15:51.390
That idiot!

00:15:51.390 --> 00:15:53.030
Don't you think it's rude?

00:15:53.030 --> 00:15:55.680
That soldier, Maeda?

00:15:55.680 --> 00:15:58.320
It's his job; he can't help it.

00:15:58.320 --> 00:16:02.700
And I hear that Yoshiwara
is no place for a lady to go alone.

00:16:02.700 --> 00:16:05.830
It's fine! I'm hot on the trail of a mystery.

00:16:05.830 --> 00:16:08.420
But is it all right for you to be here?

00:16:08.420 --> 00:16:12.380
Yeah. The editor-in-chief
doesn't listen to a thing I say.

00:16:12.380 --> 00:16:17.550
I was working on the bodies in Yoshiwara,
and he sent me to the Imperial Hotel.

00:16:20.140 --> 00:16:21.800
What's that look for?

00:16:21.800 --> 00:16:25.560
I just remembered that rude guy, Rufus!

00:16:25.560 --> 00:16:28.480
As if this perfume would ever be popular.

00:16:28.480 --> 00:16:30.850
It doesn't even smell that good.

00:16:33.610 --> 00:16:37.110
You're right. It has a cloying sweetness.

00:16:37.110 --> 00:16:40.780
Huh? I think it stinks so bad,
my nose can barely take it.

00:16:40.780 --> 00:16:42.780
Listen, would you give this to me?

00:16:42.780 --> 00:16:43.490
Please.

00:16:43.490 --> 00:16:45.200
Well, yeah, okay.

00:16:45.200 --> 00:16:46.910
I don't even like it.

00:16:46.910 --> 00:16:48.290
Thank you.

00:16:50.540 --> 00:16:52.290
I see.

00:16:56.910 --> 00:16:59.760
Yamagami here. Vamp found.

00:16:59.760 --> 00:17:01.050
Found!

00:17:02.630 --> 00:17:04.340
No answer, huh?

00:17:06.470 --> 00:17:09.510
Vampires. Vampires!

00:17:09.510 --> 00:17:11.900
There are two roads open to you!

00:17:11.900 --> 00:17:12.900
One!

00:17:12.900 --> 00:17:18.190
Obey us, Special Forces Unit 16,
and you will receive blood and...

00:17:18.190 --> 00:17:21.270
Hey, are you even listening to me?

00:17:21.270 --> 00:17:25.020
Hey! If you can hear me, say something!

00:17:25.020 --> 00:17:28.280
Can't they talk?

00:17:28.280 --> 00:17:30.460
Stay back! This gun's the latest model!

00:17:30.460 --> 00:17:32.570
It can even kill you!

00:17:36.740 --> 00:17:39.370
Hey, stop that!

00:17:39.370 --> 00:17:40.870
Don't bite my arm!

00:17:40.870 --> 00:17:42.930
Unranked blood is bitter!

00:17:42.930 --> 00:17:44.390
Don't bite me!

00:17:48.090 --> 00:17:49.050
Yamagami?!

00:17:49.050 --> 00:17:50.050
What's wrong?

00:17:50.050 --> 00:17:52.390
I heard the major's voice, but faintly!

00:17:52.390 --> 00:17:52.960
I'm going!

00:17:52.960 --> 00:17:54.090
Kurusu!

00:17:54.090 --> 00:17:59.650
I believe prostitutes who die of illness
are left at a temple over that way.

00:17:59.650 --> 00:18:02.520
No one would go near a place like that.

00:18:02.520 --> 00:18:04.200
We'll hurry to that temple.

00:18:04.200 --> 00:18:05.860
Tell Suwa, too.

00:18:05.860 --> 00:18:06.770
Maeda!

00:18:06.770 --> 00:18:07.700
What?

00:18:07.700 --> 00:18:09.320
Look at that.

00:18:13.990 --> 00:18:16.710
Special Forces Unit 16! Blockade Yoshiwara!

00:18:18.330 --> 00:18:20.790
Major! Major Yamagami!

00:18:20.790 --> 00:18:22.370
They're all vampires?

00:18:23.370 --> 00:18:26.390
Yamagami! You're okay!

00:18:26.390 --> 00:18:29.340
You're late, Kurusu.

00:18:29.340 --> 00:18:32.180
I'm going to run out of blood.

00:18:32.180 --> 00:18:34.300
Get away from Yamagami!

00:18:41.940 --> 00:18:45.450
That softness will get your friends killed.

00:18:45.450 --> 00:18:47.520
Stop!

00:19:03.460 --> 00:19:05.250
Did I...?

00:19:05.250 --> 00:19:07.180
You were too late.

00:19:07.180 --> 00:19:10.500
What would you have done if I died?

00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:12.460
I'll be faster next time!

00:19:20.600 --> 00:19:23.440
You're incredible, Kurusu.

00:19:47.750 --> 00:19:49.430
Akesato.

00:19:57.220 --> 00:19:58.940
I'm returning this.

00:20:03.440 --> 00:20:07.060
Mister... sing.

00:20:09.020 --> 00:20:10.770
I...

00:20:10.770 --> 00:20:14.950
...really don't know any songs.

00:20:14.950 --> 00:20:17.110
You're nice.

00:20:30.250 --> 00:20:34.590
What are you doing here, Suwa?

00:20:34.590 --> 00:20:38.390
Oh, what a waste of a young body.

00:20:38.390 --> 00:20:39.840
Hey, Takeuchi.

00:20:39.840 --> 00:20:40.940
Yes?

00:20:45.350 --> 00:20:49.980
If you know any songs, would you teach me one?

00:20:58.410 --> 00:20:59.740
Colonel Maeda!

00:20:59.740 --> 00:21:01.820
Yamagami's alive!

00:21:01.820 --> 00:21:04.670
I needed Kurusu to save my bacon.

00:21:04.670 --> 00:21:06.040
Kurusu did this?

00:21:06.040 --> 00:21:07.790
I just got desperate and...

00:21:09.790 --> 00:21:11.430
I see.

00:21:11.430 --> 00:21:13.930
What, sir?

00:21:13.930 --> 00:21:15.140
Nothing.

00:21:20.640 --> 00:21:24.050
The promise was not to make
Tokyo a hunting ground.

00:21:24.050 --> 00:21:28.060
I'll relay your message to my masters.

00:21:28.060 --> 00:21:30.980
I want to pass my nights in peace.

00:21:35.660 --> 00:21:36.780
I see.

00:21:36.780 --> 00:21:38.950
So that's what it was.

00:21:38.950 --> 00:21:40.240
What is it?

00:21:40.240 --> 00:21:42.990
They were moving it disguised as liquor barrels.

00:21:42.990 --> 00:21:44.920
Where did it come from?

00:21:44.920 --> 00:21:46.490
Liquor, huh?

00:21:48.460 --> 00:21:51.330
That smells like Scotch.

00:21:51.330 --> 00:21:53.430
Which means Great Britain.

00:21:53.430 --> 00:21:58.520
Anywhere Scotch might be
brought from Britain is suspicious.

00:21:58.520 --> 00:22:00.230
I'll have special forces track--

00:22:04.440 --> 00:22:06.310
Maeda?

00:22:06.310 --> 00:22:07.650
Maeda!

00:22:08.900 --> 00:22:10.100
Maeda!

00:23:41.990 --> 00:23:46.990
Persona Non Grata
